# Implement MPU-6050 Accelerometer for Crash Detection

Based on your schematic, your tracker uses an **MPU-6050** Accelerometer/Gyroscope. We will implement it to detect high G-force impacts (accidents/crashes) and immediately alert the system.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Hardware Dependency**
> You will need to install the **Adafruit MPU6050** and **Adafruit Unified Sensor** libraries in your Arduino IDE before uploading the code.

> [!NOTE]
> **Crash Threshold**
> I plan to set the crash detection threshold to **3.5G** (approx 34 m/s²). If you want this to be more or less sensitive, please let me know!

## Proposed Changes

### ESP32 Tracker Firmware

#### [NEW] [Accelerometer.ino](file:///c:/Users/Projects/Desktop/Unizik%20Tracker/ESP32_Tracker/Accelerometer.ino)
- Create a new file to manage the MPU-6050.
- Initialize I2C communication on pins 21 (SDA) and 22 (SCL).
- Continuously read the X, Y, and Z accelerometer values.
- Calculate the total acceleration vector magnitude: `sqrt(x² + y² + z²)`.
- If magnitude > 34 m/s² (3.5G), publish an MQTT alert to `pathfinder/alerts` with `type: "crash"` and trigger a 10-second cooldown so it doesn't spam alerts.

#### [MODIFY] [ESP32_Tracker.ino](file:///c:/Users/Projects/Desktop/Unizik%20Tracker/ESP32_Tracker/ESP32_Tracker.ino)
- Call `setupAccelerometer()` inside `setup()`.
- Call `loopAccelerometer()` inside `loop()`.

